//============================================================================================================================================
//                                                            SLATEUI.SYMBOLINDEX
//============================================================================================================================================
// 🧩 Symbol roll for SlateUI — Vector glyphs rasterised once and keyed by content — two names sharing bytes share one texture, and no vendor identity escapes.

%format   symbolindex 1.0
%scope    layer
%path     Engine/SlateUI
%folders  7
%symbols  85

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     FOLDER INDEXES
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 21 sym | Vector glyphs rasterised once and keyed by content — two names sharing bytes share one texture, and no vendor identity escapes.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym | The one seam the interface library crosses — device handles in, recorded commands out, no ImGui spelling.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 9 sym  | The only translation unit in the engine that includes ImGui.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym | Presents RowSequence through RankIndex and writes intent back — holding no relation of its own.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 15 sym | The counted span presented, and every gesture over it turned into a declared intent.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 10 sym | The one palette and the one set of layout extents every panel reads — resolved once a tick, held by nobody else.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 10 sym | The one translation unit in which an interface colour literal and a layout extent literal are permitted.

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                        SYMBOLS
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

T GlyphHandle                           | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 28-35   | An opaque reference to one uploaded glyph, resolved to a vendor texture identity inside the source file alone. an integer whose meaning only `GlyphDepot.cpp` knows, exactly as `InterfaceExchange` holds its context.
F GlyphHandle::HandleDeclared           | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 34      | Whether this handle names an uploaded glyph at all.
T GlyphAttachment                       | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 45-51   | The device handles one upload needs, supplied once at bring-up. recording, and every allocation here happens inside `Declare` — which is bring-up, never a tick.
T GlyphDeclaration                      | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 61-67   | One glyph as a tier declares it — its key, its vector source, and the square it rasterises into. span may name a string literal in the declaring translation unit.
T GlyphTier                             | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 74-79   | A named set of glyphs one workspace declares at activation. edits nothing shared. The chrome tier is declared once and read by every workspace; content-hash dedup means a glyph two tiers share uploads once and is torn down when the second releases it.
T GlyphDepot                            | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 92-204  | A store of rasterised, evictable, reconstructible glyphs keyed by the content that produced them. tiers share a glyph while each keeps its own name. Collapsing it to key-to-texture uploads the chrome twisty once per workspace, and the count grows with the workspace count rather than with the art. at workspace activation and a resolution during a tick never allocates.
F GlyphDepot::~GlyphDepot               | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 99      | ?
F GlyphDepot::Construct                 | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 108     | Attaches the depot to a device and brings the vector rasteriser up. when the rasteriser declines to start
F GlyphDepot::Reclaim                   | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 115     | Destroys every uploaded glyph and releases the rasteriser. reads after it was freed, and the read succeeds often enough to look like a different defect.
F GlyphDepot::Declare                   | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 126     | Declares one whole tier, rasterising and uploading what is not already held. and with ExtentExhausted when an upload could not be claimed to compare a tier's declaration list against what resolves, one key at a time.
F GlyphDepot::Release                   | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 134     | Releases one tier's claim on its glyphs, tearing down those no other tier still names.
F GlyphDepot::Resolve                   | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 142     | Resolves one key to its handle.
F GlyphDepot::GlyphHeld                 | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 147     | Whether one key resolves to an uploaded glyph.
F GlyphDepot::DeclaredEdge              | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 152     | The square edge a declaration that names none rasterises into.
F GlyphDepot::DeclareEdge               | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 160     | Declares the square edge a declaration that names none rasterises into.
F GlyphDepot::UploadedCount             | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 167     | How many distinct textures the depot holds — what dedup is measured against. the two-level indirection exists for.
F GlyphDepot::KeyCount                  | Api/GlyphDepot.h              | 172     | How many keys resolve.
